2:T56d,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do prices start \"from\" a figure instead of a fixed price?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The starting figure reflects the smallest realistic version of that service. Actual cost depends on scope — number of data sources, pages, integrations, or branches involved. You get an exact, written price after the discovery call, before any commitment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you require full payment upfront?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Projects are typically split into milestone payments tied to agreed stages of delivery, so you are never paying in full for work not yet done."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a retainer option for ongoing work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. For businesses that expect regular changes, new reports, or support, a monthly retainer is available and is discussed once the first project is delivered and you know what ongoing support you actually need."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is not included in the starting price?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Third-party costs — such as premium Power BI licensing for very large teams, paid API access some integrations require, or hosting fees — are identified during scoping and are never a hidden surprise at the end."}}]}e:X
